     Tterm - a simple terminal program for OS9 and OS9000             by Stephen Carville Contents:       readme - this file        tterm - executable          tsu - quick setup program for Tterm.    tterm.doc - documentaion for Tterm.              xyt - program to provide X and Y transfers services.      xyt.doc - documentation for xyt.  All of the programs in this archive were compiled using the Microware Ultra-C compiler.  They require the 'csl' module and, if no Math  Coprocessor is available the module 'fpu' for OS9/68000 system or 'fpuem' for OS9/x86 systems.   If you do not already have these modules, archives containing them and  instructions for installing are available from:           Delphi - OS9 forum in the OSK System Modules database    Compuserve - OS9 forum  via anonymous FTP from     os9archive.rtsi.com/OS9/MISC/ucc_support_68k.uue    os9archive.rtsi.com/OS9/OS9000/CMDS/ucc_support_OS9000.lzh This program is brought to you by:     Stephen Carville    P.O. Box 822     Glendora, CA 91740 USA    (818) 914-2511    pagan@delphi.com  Custom modification to this or any other of my programs is available.   Contact me at the above phone number or E-mail address for further  information.  